      "content": "It takes a difficult amount of courage to feel this way about oneself, and many people who see themselves this way later realize that this guilt has distorted their self-view rather than telling the truth about their actions. Your perspective that you are just \"taking up space\" might be an oversimplification of a much more complex human experience shaped by trauma, fear, or past conditioning. What feels like self-loathing today could actually be a signal from you that you deserve more understanding and compassion toward your past self than you currently have for yourself.",
